            <Comment Type="public">Combination treatment of BRAF inhibitor dabrafenib and MEK inhibitor trametinib is recommended for adjuvant treatment of stage III or recurrent melanoma with the less common BRAF V600K mutation detected by the approved THxID kit, as well as first line treatment for metastatic melanoma. This treatment combination was FDA approved based on the (COMBI-v) trial, where 68 V600K metastatic melanoma patients had either a 65 percent response rate to dabrafenib and trametinib combination therapy, or a 44 percent with vemurafenib alone (civic.EID:4181), as well as the COMBI-D (civic.EID:6939), and COMBI-AD (civic.EID:6179) Trials, which also showed superiority of combination therapy.</Comment>
